{"id":"80877ec6-88aa-46ae-9bb6-71a9550b5823","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.09.023","title":"A spatiotemporal lifecycle atlas decodes spatial coordination in rice","title_zh":"一份时空生命周期图谱揭示水稻空间协调机制","doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2026.09.023","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.09.023","abstract":"How gene expression programs are coordinated across space and time to build a complete plant remains poorly understood. Here, we combine high-resolution spatial transcriptomics, single-nucleus RNA sequencing, and a gap-free reference genome to build a 3D spatiotemporal atlas of rice, spanning 10 organs and 61 stages from seed to seed. Our datasets profile 851,725 nuclei and 347,640 spatial bins, defining 119 cell types and 133 subtypes across the rice lifecycle. Through multimodal integration, we reconstruct an inferred developmental trajectory graph that links cell states from the proembryo to mature organs and identifies trajectory-associated regulators. We further implicate the pleiotropic regulator OsARF1 in distinct spatial gene programs across developmental contexts. We also uncover widespread axis-associated transcriptional asymmetry, including dorsoventral endosperm programs that partition starch and protein accumulation. Collectively, this high-resolution atlas provides a spatiotemporal framework for understanding rice development and guiding future crop improvement.","abstract_zh":"关于基因表达程序如何在空间和时间上协调以构建完整植物的机制尚不清楚。本文结合高分辨率空间转录组学、单核RNA测序以及无缺口参考基因组，构建了覆盖10个器官、61个阶段（从种子到种子）的水稻3D时空图谱。数据集共分析了851,725个细胞核和347,640个空间区块，定义了119种细胞类型和133种亚型。通过多模态整合，我们重建了一个推断的发育轨迹图，连接了从原胚到成熟器官的细胞状态，并识别了与轨迹相关的调控因子。进一步发现多效性调控因子OsARF1在不同发育背景下参与不同空间基因程序。我们还揭示了广泛的轴向转录不对称性，包括背腹胚乳程序在淀粉和蛋白质积累上的分区。总体而言，这份高分辨率图谱为理解水稻发育提供了时空框架，并为未来作物改良提供指导。","snippet":"How gene expression programs are coordinated across space and time to build a complete plant remains poorly understood. Here, we combine high-resolution spatial transcriptomics, single-nucleus RNA sequencing, and a gap-free reference genome to build a 3D spatiotemporal atlas of rice, spanning 10 organs and 61 stages from seed to seed. Our datasets profile 851,725 nuclei and 347,640 spatial bins, defining 119 cell ty…","translated_at":"2026-10-07T23:32:39.490153+00:00","translation_model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":null,"issue":null,"published_at":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-10-06T20:47:26Z","display_date":"2026-10-06T20:47:26Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":null,"print_published_at":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Yi Jing","authors_text":"Yi Jing, Qiong Chen, Yifan Chen, Wei Yan, Yuejing Gui, Yicheng Zhong, Mumu Qin, Han Zhang, James Whelan, Chuanxiu Li, Shiyu Chen, Chunyan Xu, Weiming He, Zhiyao Lv, Feng Yang, Rouxi Chen, Jing Zhang, Zongan Wang, Zhenyu Xiong, Xun Liao, Keke Xia, Tong Wei, Longjiang Fan, Tao Yang, Yinqi Bai, Jiwei Xu, Ying Dai, Fang Zhang, Shenhui Yang, Yanting Qiao, Shengwu Xiong, Yi Rong, Cunman He, Huixia Shou, Lei Wang, Qian Wang, Xueqing Xia, Xiongbo Peng, Kaiting Sun, Yongzhong Xing, Lin Du, Rui Han, Chao Qin, Likun Jiang, Xinsen Yang, Jun'e Jiang, Xinle Yu, Jiantao Wu, Rui Li, Yinru Yan, Yizhou Wang, Ying Gu, Jian Wang, Pengfei Jia, Xiaodong Fang, Peng Zhao, Zhen Yue, Hongwei Guo, Yidan Ouyang, Xun Xu, Fan Chen","authors":[{"position":0,"given_name":"Yi","family_name":"Jing","full_name":"Yi Jing","affiliation":null},{"position":1,"given_name":"Qiong","family_name":"Chen","full_name":"Qiong Chen","affiliation":null},{"position":2,"given_name":"Yifan","family_name":"Chen","full_name":"Yifan Chen","affiliation":null},{"position":3,"given_name":"Wei","family_name":"Yan","full_name":"Wei Yan","affiliation":null},{"position":4,"given_name":"Yuejing","family_name":"Gui","full_name":"Yuejing Gui","affiliation":null},{"position":5,"given_name":"Yicheng","family_name":"Zhong","full_name":"Yicheng Zhong","affiliation":null},{"position":6,"given_name":"Mumu","family_name":"Qin","full_name":"Mu